"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Florence County runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. That pair is also the driest, with a normal of 5.74 inches, though on the middle it ran 137% of normal in 2025. In 2026 so far, March to April came in at 24% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 17000 had its driest year in 1954 at 63%.</p>"}
